# kprobes.fragment — enable KPROBES on the merlin 4.19 GT-BE98 kernel
#
# Verified working 2026-06-24 (built a pkgtb with register_kprobe in System.map).
# Purpose: kprobe the CLOSED stock dhd binary (e.g. its WLC_UP / -110 wedge path)
# from a kernel module — kprobes is the only way to trace a binary blob.
#
# Apply with scripts/configure-kernel.sh:
#   scripts/configure-kernel.sh config-fragments/kprobes.fragment
# It merges this onto the base defconfig and runs `make olddefconfig`.
#
# This is a standard kbuild config fragment (the same format merge_config.sh
# consumes). The third line is OPTIONAL: enabling CONFIG_KPROBES exposes
# CONFIG_KPROBES_SANITY_TEST, but `olddefconfig` resolves newly-exposed symbols
# to their default (off) automatically — no manual pinning, no "Unexpected EOF".
# We keep it explicit only to document intent. CONFIG_OPTPROBES is def_bool and
# is likewise auto-resolved.

CONFIG_KPROBES=y
CONFIG_KALLSYMS_ALL=y
# CONFIG_KPROBES_SANITY_TEST is not set
